  "summary": "ToeJam & Earl in Panic on Funkotron is Johnson Voorsanger Productions' platform game, first released for Genesis in North America in December 1993.",
  "body": [
    "ToeJam & Earl in Panic on Funkotron is Johnson Voorsanger Productions' platform game, first released for Genesis in North America in December 1993. After returning home, ToeJam and Earl discover that Earthlings have stowed away on their ship and are causing trouble on Funkotron. One or two players search the planet, capture the visitors in jars and arrange their return to Earth. The sequel exchanges the original game's overhead exploration for side-scrolling stages, bringing its comic aliens into a more direct platforming structure while retaining cooperative play.",
    "The Earthlings hide throughout each area, so simply reaching the far side does not finish the job. A radar helps locate visitors that remain out of sight, and throwing jars captures them after the player has found a suitable position. Clearing the area allows the pair to continue. Presents provide useful bonuses, including equipment that helps with the search or movement. The task gives each stage a reason to explore its platforms and concealed corners, with two players able to share the search and deal with troublesome visitors together.",
    "Funkotron also contains musical diversions and hidden places that interrupt the capture mission. Jam Out and the Fungus Olympics turn a detour into a small separate challenge, while the HyperFunk Zone offers another unusual space to discover. Collecting objects associated with Lamont contributes to the best ending. These extras preserve the sense that ToeJam and Earl inhabit a place with its own habits and pleasures. The sequel's more conventional platform structure becomes a setting for that personality, with the invading humans supplying much of its humour and the search giving cooperation a clear purpose."
  ],
